# Copy to .env.local and fill in both values.
#
# Primary path — an ampd node an operator runs for you; you do not run one.
# Ask your amp contact for the node URL and the board planet tag
# (README "Run Against an Operated Node").

# The operated node's app.www URL, e.g. https://<operated-node>
VITE_AMP_VAULT_URL=
# Board planet tag or UID, handed to you with the node URL.
VITE_AMP_PLANET_TAG=

# ─── Self-hosted dev only — AMP-internal, not part of a web-SDK integration ───
# Only if you build ampd yourself (README "Run Against a Local ampd").  Swap the
# pair above for these: a local ampd serves app.www on port 5193, and logs the
# board UID at boot — "forums custodian ready: board planet <UID> (public)".
#
# VITE_AMP_VAULT_URL=http://localhost:5193
# VITE_AMP_PLANET_TAG=
